# Arm the camera to image each umbra
# Turns on the camera's supply, psu2 CH1, sets each exposure from the umbra's length
# and turns umbra captures on. From here the camera images each time the orbit the
# run follows enters the Earth's shadow, and stops when it leaves. Choose the orbit
# first, with orbit follow or orbit replay. Each image is tagged with TC01, so load
# rSMTC08 too. psu2 is disabled in the shipped hardware map: enable it in the live
# usbmap.json before a run.
block detector imaging
load rSLTA rOrbit rPSU

slta startup
slta nsamp 10
slta exposure 600
slta run on
